  "notes": "The HTTP/1 pull BodyReader drives the existing push parser through a bounded FIFO producer. Tests cover a 200 KiB body with 100-continue and keep-alive, chunked trailers, cancellation closing an unread connection, max_body_bytes rejection, and non-blocking takeRequest. HTTP/2 ServerDuplexStream.nextBody pulls DATA, retains trailers for requestTrailers, and returns null at END_STREAM. HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 concurrent batch aliases are exposed through netz.streaming."
